In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful

Member of the People's Majlis

[signature] 03/08/2026

Motion submitted under Article 101(a) of the Constitution of the Republic of Maldives and Section 229(a) of the Rules of Procedure of the People's Majlis for a vote of no confidence in the Minister of Economic Development, Transport and Trade, Mohamed Saeed

This is a motion to remove from office, under Article 101(a) of the Constitution, the Minister of Economic Development, Transport and Trade, Mohamed Saeed, a member of the Cabinet appointed by the President under the Constitution of the Republic of Maldives, because he has acted clearly contrary to the Constitution in carrying out the responsibilities entrusted to Cabinet members under Article 132 of the Constitution, and because confidence in the Minister has been lost as he has neglected the duty to be accountable to the People's Majlis under Articles 98 and 134 of the Constitution.

Whereas Article 132(b) of the Constitution states that every member of the Cabinet [unclear] all matters in the areas within the responsibilities of that ministry [unclear] and must be accountable [unclear] for matters relating to that member's responsibilities;

Whereas Article 98 of the Constitution states that a member of the Cabinet may be summoned to the People's Majlis and must answer the questions put by the People's Majlis concerning the post and responsibilities that person holds [unclear];

Whereas under Article 134 of the Constitution, members of the Cabinet must be accountable to the People's Majlis, as set out in the Constitution, in carrying out the responsibilities, duties and activities entrusted to them, and every member of the Cabinet must provide the People's Majlis with any information it requires on matters [unclear] within that member's jurisdiction;

Whereas a member of the Cabinet is prohibited from using the influence of his office, or information obtained by virtue of his office, to advance his own interests or those of another person, and the powers of the office must be used only in the public interest;

[stamp: People's Majlis Secretariat; 2505; Dhunain; 13:05; 3.8.26; D] [signature] 3/8/2026

Given the matters stated above, while he contravenes the responsibilities entrusted to Cabinet members under Article 132 of the Constitution and commits acts obstructing accountability to the Majlis under Articles 98 and 134 of the Constitution;

We, the undersigned members, submit to the People's Majlis, under Article 101(a) of the Constitution of the Republic of Maldives, the motion of no confidence in the Minister of Economic Development, Transport and Trade, Mohamed Saeed, requesting his removal from office.

3 August 2026
